-- title:
--   Corepresentability of a conjugation-quotient deformation subfunctor
-- statement:
--   Let $n$ be a finite type, $G$ a topological group, and $\mathcal{O}$ a commutative local ring with finite residue field; let $F$ be a subfunctor of the functor [`Deformation.repnFunctor n G 𝓞`](def/Deformations_LiftFunctor.html#L18) on the category [`Deformation.ProartinianCat 𝓞`](def/Deformations_ProartinianCat.html#L44) of local pro-Artinian topological $\mathcal{O}$-algebras with residue field that of $\mathcal{O}$, which sends an object $R$ to the set of continuous monoid homomorphisms $G \to \mathrm{GL}_n(R)$ and a morphism to post-composition with the induced map on invertible matrices. Four hypotheses are assumed. First, `ConjStable`: for every object $A$, every $\rho' \in F(A)$ and every $\gamma$ in `conjKer A`, the subgroup of $\mathrm{ConjAct}(\mathrm{GL}_n(A))$ of elements whose underlying matrix lies in the kernel of $\mathrm{GL}_n(A) \to \mathrm{GL}_n(k)$ for the residue field $k$ of $A$, one has $\gamma \cdot \rho' \in F(A)$. Second, `ReflectedByInjective`: for every morphism $\iota : T \to A$ with injective underlying map and every $\sigma : G \to \mathrm{GL}_n(T)$, if the push-forward of $\sigma$ along $\iota$ lies in $F(A)$ then $\sigma \in F(T)$. Third, the category of elements of $F$ has a weakly initial object, i.e. there is an element $T$ admitting at least one morphism to every element. Fourth, every $\rho' \in F(A)$ satisfies `TraceAlgebra.Descends`: some $\gamma \in$ `conjKer A` makes all matrix entries of $(\gamma \cdot \rho')(g)$, for all $g \in G$, lie in `traceSubalgebra 𝓞 ρ'`, the topological closure of the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra generated by the traces of $\rho'$. The conclusion is that the functor underlying `conjQuotSubfunctor n F`, namely $R \mapsto$ the image of $F(R)$ in the quotient of $G \to \mathrm{GL}_n(R)$ by the conjugation action of `conjKer R`, is corepresentable, i.e. isomorphic to the functor of morphisms out of some local pro-Artinian $\mathcal{O}$-algebra.
--
--   This is the general existence statement for a universal deformation ring of a given deformation type: the conjugation-quotient of a deformation condition $F$ is corepresented by an object of the pro-Artinian category, provided $F$ is conjugation-stable, reflected along injections, weakly initial-bounded, and satisfies trace descent. It is applied in [`GaloisRep.nonempty_deformationRingData`](thm.html#GaloisRep.nonempty_deformationRingData) to produce the deformation-ring data used in the modularity-lifting argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Deformation_isCorepresentable_conjQuotSubfunctor_of_descends.lean

import Mathlib
